ource>Nature.</source> <volume>355</volume>:<fpage>696</fpage>&#x02013;702.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1741056</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Ilsley, J.L., M. Sudol, and S.J. Winder. <year>2001</year>. The interaction of dystrophin with beta-dystroglycan is regulated by tyrosine phosphorylation. <source>Cell. Signal.</source> <volume>13</volume>:<fpage>625</fpage>&#x02013;632.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11495720</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Ilsley, J.L., M. Sudol, and S.J. Winder. <year>2002</year>. The WW domain: linking cell signalling to the membrane cytoskeleton. <source>Cell. Signal.</source> <volume>14</volume>:<fpage>183</fpage>&#x02013;189.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11812645</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">James, M., A. Nuttall, J.L. Ilsley, K. Ottersbach, J.M. Tinsley, M. Sudol, and S.J. Winder. <year>2000</year>. Adhesion-dependent tyrosine phosphorylation of (beta)-dystroglycan regulates its interaction with utrophin. <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>113</volume>:<fpage>1717</fpage>&#x02013;1726.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10769203</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Lunter, P.C., and G. Wiche. <year>2002</year>. Direct binding of plectin to Fer kinase and negative regulation of its catalytic activity. <source>Biochem. Biophys. Res. Commun.</source> <volume>296</volume>:<fpage>904</fpage>&#x02013;910.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12200133</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Newey, S.E., E.V. Howman, C.P. Ponting, M.A. Benson, R. Nawrotzki, N.Y. Loh, K.E. Davies, and D.J. Blake. <year>2001</year>. Syncoilin, a novel member of the intermediate filament superfamily that interacts with alpha-dystrobrevin in skeletal muscle. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>276</volume>:<fpage>6645</fpage>&#x02013;6655.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11053421</pub-id><